    credit: "Moshe Marlin Levin / Meitar Collection / National Library of Israel
      / The Pritzker Family National Photography Collection \xB7 CC BY 4.0 \xB7 graded
      and cropped"
    sensitive: 0
    sensitivityReviewed: 0
  - eventId: frumkin_commission
    image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9ac6b7418fe5f408a9d7be0e1c317ec0, type: 3}
    alt: Snow and slush at the Ras al-Ein (Rosh HaAyin) immigrant camp, winter 1950.
    credit: "Benno Rothenberg / Meitar Collection / National Library of Israel /
      The Pritzker Family National Photography Collection / Israel State Archives
      \xB7 CC BY 4.0 \xB7 graded and cropped"
    sensitive: 0
    sensitivityReviewed: 0
  - eventId: hula_drainage
    image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 8667fce6f8c2b4633b2e291e9cdddd07, type: 3}
    alt: Timber shuttering and earthworks for the dams that drained Lake Hula, 1951.
